    "reasoning": "The earlier selected answers remain mathematically correct and are established by each question's own captured solution. For q-29556, solve 2x-\\pi/6=n\\pi. For q-81546, solve 6x+\\pi/2=\\pi/2+n\\pi, giving x=n\\pi/6; the choice omits only 'x='. Its option 2 is also mathematically equivalent because \\pi/2+n\\pi/6=(n+3)\\pi/6. Thus that question contains duplicate valid choices, although option 0 matches the source's stated expression directly; grading of option 2 is unavailable. For q-29349, solve 2x=90°+180°n. For q-117698, solve 4x+\\pi/4=\\pi/2+n\\pi. For q-41106 and q-26063, exclude inputs satisfying 3x+\\pi/6=\\pi/2+n\\pi and 2x=\\pi/2+n\\pi, respectively. Infinitely many solutions require matching coefficients and constants: q-288436 gives p=2; q-287970 gives p=3/2; q-288622 gives m=5, n=3 and m+n=8; q-288627 gives p=8, q=20 and p+q=28. Altitudes are perpendicular segments from the opposite vertex to the specified side's line: q-118692 uses QP; q-77606 uses the perpendicular from C to AB; q-52943 uses the perpendicular from B to extended AC; q-67742 uses the perpendicular from A to extended BC. For q-27832, the supplementary angle is 70°, so the requested angle is 90°-70°=20°. For q-118757, the supplementary angle is 62°, so the requested angle is 90°-62°=28°. No revealed grade contradicts these answers.",
